ly  introducted  virus is more or less similar to  a coronavirus which is more or less  frequent  in the children population now the  the mutations are something new for the  immune system and that probably one  reason why  the numbers are going up but it's not  good underst and there's not a good  understanding how  how this this works so  do we then know whether all children are  equally at risk right now or  especially those with a special  precondition  well good news is that most of the  children  do not have a very high risk to to  become seriously illness but um  there are also complicated um some  complications especially in those  children which are  risk and those children are new bonds or  preterm infants or  those with underlying diseases for  example congenital heart deficiency or  immunodeficiencies um as well as those  children which were treated with  immunocompromising medications in term  in terms of hemato oncological diseases  and so on  there is a relevant number of children  with  a high risk and one prominent a  group of diseases um the  down syndrome those children are at very  high risk  for severe and fatal outcome  um due to sask of two and other children  with  um let's say  inborn era of metabolisms or  syndromes for example like tuberose  sclerosis and others  and these children uh they react  differently mostly  to the virus than adults or elderly uh  with with inflammatory uh reactions of  various organs i mean how  worried should we be about the so-called  pims or misc  yeah this inflammatory multi system  syndrome is is not very common  so we do have observations of this  syndrome  in in hospitals especially in my  hospital  as well but the numbers are overall  um overall the numbers are though so  there is  not really a matter to worry about this  but  at least there are some children which  were affected by these pims  and there is an assumption that a  genetically  determined susceptibility um  is responsible for these cases so t